---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Try HVAC Boot Camp | Matter: Solids, Liquids, and Gases"
  description="Try a short, phone-first HVAC Boot Camp lesson about matter, solids, liquids, and gases before deciding whether to enroll."
>
  <div class="trial-page">
    <section class="trial-intro">
      <div class="trial-intro-inner">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Free lesson preview</p><h1>See how Boot Camp helps when a concept does not click.</h1><p>This short preview uses the opening Unit 1 concept. Work through it on your phone or computer—no account required.</p></div>
        <div class="trial-meta"><span>Unit 1</span><strong>Matter: Solids, Liquids, and Gases</strong><small>Preview · about 3 minutes</small></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="trial-workspace">
      <article class="lesson-phone" aria-labelledby="lesson-title">
        <header class="lesson-phone-header">
          <div><span>Unit 1 · Foundations</span><strong>Page 1 of 8</strong></div>
          <div class="lesson-progress"><span></span></div>
        </header>

        <div class="lesson-body">
          <p class="preview-kicker">One idea</p>
          <h2 id="lesson-title">Matter normally appears as a solid, liquid, or gas.</h2>
          <p class="lesson-lead">Matter is anything that has mass and takes up space. The three common states behave differently:</p>

          <div class="state-grid">
            <div><span class="state-icon solid-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>Solid</strong><p>Keeps its shape and volume.</p><small>Example: a wrench</small></div>
            <div><span class="state-icon liquid-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>Liquid</strong><p>Keeps its volume but changes shape.</p><small>Example: drain-pan water</small></div>
            <div><span class="state-icon gas-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>Gas</strong><p>Changes shape and volume.</p><small>Example: air in ductwork</small></div>
          </div>

          <div class="lesson-help" aria-labelledby="help-title">
            <p id="help-title">Choose the help you need</p>
            <div class="help-buttons">
              <button type="button" data-help="simple">Explain it simply</button>
              <button type="button" data-help="example">Give me an HVAC example</button>
              <button type="button" data-help="why">Why does this matter?</button>
            </div>
            <div class="help-response" data-response="simple" hidden><strong>A simpler way:</strong><p>A solid stays put. A liquid can pour. A gas spreads out to fill the space around it.</p></div>
            <div class="help-response" data-response="example" hidden><strong>HVAC example:</strong><p>A copper fitting is a solid, water in a drain pan is a liquid, and air moving through a supply duct is a gas.</p></div>
            <div class="help-response" data-response="why" hidden><strong>Why technicians need this:</strong><p>HVAC systems move heat by controlling matter. Air carries heat through ductwork, refrigerant changes between liquid and gas, and solid metal transfers heat through coils and tubing.</p></div>
          </div>

          <form class="quick-check" data-quick-check>
            <fieldset>
              <legend><span>Quick check</span>Water is poured from a glass into a drain pan. What changes?</legend>
              <label><input type="radio" name="matter-check" value="volume" /> Its volume</label>
              <label><input type="radio" name="matter-check" value="shape" /> Its shape</label>
              <label><input type="radio" name="matter-check" value="both" /> Both</label>
            </fieldset>
            <button class="button button-dark" type="submit">Check my answer</button>
            <p class="check-feedback" data-check-feedback aria-live="polite"></p>
          </form>
        </div>
      </article>

      <aside class="trial-decision">
        <p class="eyebrow">What this preview demonstrates</p>
        <h2>Short content. Useful choices. Immediate feedback.</h2>
        <p>The complete Unit 1 pilot is still under review. This page demonstrates the approved learning rhythm without pretending that the live AI tutor is finished.</p>
        <ul class="plain-check-list"><li>One concept per page</li><li>HVAC examples instead of generic examples</li><li>Help without leaving the lesson</li><li>A quick check before moving on</li></ul>
        <div class="trial-next-card"><strong>Like the approach?</strong><p>Review the complete Boot Camp and decide whether the course fits your goal.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/hvac-boot-camp/">Explore HVAC Boot Camp</a><a class="text-link-dark" href="/pricing/">See plans and pricing →</a></div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="trial-footer-note">
      <p><strong>Development note:</strong> The responses on this preview page are approved scripted examples. Bounded live AI will be connected after the Unit 1 content and guardrails are approved.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    const helpButtons = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-help]");
    const responses = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-response]");

    helpButtons.forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const target = button.dataset.help;
        helpButtons.forEach((item) => item.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(item === button)));
        responses.forEach((response) => {
          response.hidden = response.dataset.response !== target;
        });
      });
    });

    const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>("[data-quick-check]");
    const feedback = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-check-feedback]");

    form?.addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      const answer = new FormData(form).get("matter-check");
      if (!feedback) return;

      if (!answer) {
        feedback.className = "check-feedback needs-answer";
        feedback.textContent = "Choose an answer first.";
      } else if (answer === "shape") {
        feedback.className = "check-feedback correct";
        feedback.textContent = "Correct. The water keeps the same volume but takes the shape of the drain pan.";
      } else {
        feedback.className = "check-feedback incorrect";
        feedback.textContent = "Not quite. The amount of water stays the same. Only its shape changes.";
      }
    });
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
